<Layout
  title="Budget Analysis MCP Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the private Budget Analysis MCP integration."
>
  <article class="prose prose-lg prose-neutral max-w-none prose-headings:font-body prose-headings:tracking-normal prose-a:text-text prose-a:underline prose-a:underline-offset-4 prose-strong:text-text">
    <h1>Budget Analysis MCP Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p><strong>Last Updated: 2026-08-07</strong></p>

    <p>
      Budget Analysis MCP (the <strong>Service</strong>) is a private, single-user integration that
      provides read-only access to one connected YNAB plan through a Model Context Protocol (MCP)
      client selected by the user. This policy explains what the Service accesses, how that data is
      used and shared, what is stored, and how it can be deleted.
    </p>

    <h2>Data the Service processes</h2>

    <p>The Service may process these categories of data:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Identity and security data:</strong> the email address and signed access assertion
        supplied by Cloudflare Access, authentication cookies or bearer tokens handled by
        Cloudflare, and request metadata needed to authenticate and protect the Service.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>YNAB financial data:</strong> account identifiers, names, types, states, balances,
        budget months, category groups, categories, assigned amounts, activity, available amounts,
        targets, payees, transaction dates, amounts, memos, clearing and approval states, flags,
        splits, transfers, and scheduled transaction definitions.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>OAuth credential data:</strong> YNAB access and refresh tokens, token expiration and
        scope, and temporary authorization state and PKCE verifier values.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Tool-request data:</strong> the read tool selected by the user and its parameters,
        such as a date range or exact account, category, payee, or transaction identifier.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The Service does not request or store credentials for bank or other financial-institution
      accounts. It does not request a YNAB password. It requests only YNAB's <code>read-only</code>
      OAuth scope.
    </p>

    <h2>How data is used</h2>

    <p>Data is used only to:</p>

    <ol>
      <li>authenticate the owner and reject every other identity;</li>
      <li>obtain and refresh read-only authorization from YNAB;</li>
      <li>make the specific YNAB API read requested through an MCP tool;</li>
      <li>validate, minimize, and format the response for budget analysis; and</li>
      <li>return that result to the MCP client the user deliberately connected.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      The Service does not use YNAB data for advertising, profiling unrelated to the requested
      budget analysis, credit decisions, or training a model operated by the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>On-demand disclosure to the selected AI client</h2>

    <p>
      When the user asks a connected AI client to call a tool, the Service returns the requested
      financial data to that client. The selected client and its provider therefore receive and may
      retain the tool result under their own terms, privacy policy, account settings, and retention
      controls.
    </p>

    <p>
      This includes OpenAI when the user connects the Service to Codex or ChatGPT. The Service sends
      data to an AI provider only in response to a tool call made through the client the user chose.
      OAuth tokens, Cloudflare assertions, cookies, and other authentication credentials are never
      included in tool results.
    </p>

    <p>
      The user should request only the data needed for the analysis and review the selected AI
      provider's data controls before connecting the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>Service providers and other disclosures</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>YNAB</strong> receives OAuth and API requests and returns the requested plan data.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare</strong> provides DNS, TLS, Access authentication, Workers execution,
        security controls, and encrypted Durable Object storage. Cloudflare may process identity,
        security, and request metadata under the operator's Cloudflare configuration and
        Cloudflare's applicable terms.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The user-selected MCP or AI client provider</strong> receives tool results only as
        described above.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      The Service does not sell or rent personal data, and it does not sell, license, aggregate, or
      analyze YNAB data for third parties. It does not share YNAB data with another user.
    </p>

    <h2>Storage, caching, and security</h2>

    <p>
      YNAB API responses and financial records are processed transiently for the current tool call.
      The Service does not persist or cache API responses, tool arguments, tool results, account
      data, budget data, or transaction data in a database, object store, or analytics system.
    </p>

    <p>
      The Service persists only the OAuth credential and authorization state needed to maintain the
      YNAB connection. Those values are stored in a Cloudflare Durable Object, whose storage
      Cloudflare encrypts at rest. Requests use HTTPS. Cloudflare Access protects the entire service
      hostname, and the Worker independently verifies the signed assertion, application audience,
      and exact owner email. Authentication headers are removed before MCP processing, and
      responses are marked <code>Cache-Control: no-store</code>.
    </p>

    <p>
      The application does not intentionally log request or response bodies, financial data, tool
      arguments, tool results, OAuth codes, cookies, or tokens. Cloudflare may retain platform and
      Access security metadata according to the Cloudflare account's settings and policies.
    </p>

    <p>
      No system can guarantee absolute security, but the Service uses these controls to limit access
      and reduce the amount and lifetime of retained data.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>
        Financial API responses remain in server memory only long enough to complete the requested
        tool call. Any copy retained by the selected MCP or AI client is governed by that provider.
      </li>
      <li>
        The active YNAB OAuth credential remains until it is replaced, permanently disconnected, or
        invalidated by a rejected refresh.
      </li>
      <li>
        Temporary OAuth state is valid for no more than 10 minutes. Its single stored record is
        replaced by a new attempt and is deleted during completion, expiry handling, or permanent
        disconnect.
      </li>
      <li>
        Cloudflare identity and security metadata follows the retention configured for the
        Cloudflare account and Cloudflare service.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Deletion and disconnection</h2>

    <p>The owner can delete credential data without contacting anyone:</p>

    <ol>
      <li>Sign in through Cloudflare Access and open the Service's connection page.</li>
      <li>
        Select <strong>Permanently disconnect</strong>. The same-origin protected action deletes the
        active credential, pending authorization state, and legacy credential-object state.
      </li>
      <li>Revoke the application's grant in YNAB to invalidate access and refresh tokens upstream.</li>
      <li>
        Remove the MCP integration and use the selected client provider's controls to delete any
        chats, tool results, or other copies retained by that provider.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      After disconnection, the Service cannot access YNAB data unless the owner completes a new
      read-only authorization.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>

    <p>The Service is private, is not offered to the public, and is not directed to children under 13.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>

    <p>
      This policy will be updated before the Service accesses a new category of YNAB data or uses or
      shares data for a new purpose. If a change materially affects YNAB data practices, the Service
      will prompt the user to consent before further access. The date at the top will identify the
      latest revision.
    </p>

    <h2>YNAB attribution</h2>

    <p>
      We are not affiliated, associated, or in any way officially connected with YNAB or any of its
      subsidiaries or affiliates. The official YNAB website can be found at
      <a href="https://www.ynab.com">https://www.ynab.com</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      The names YNAB and You Need A Budget, as well as related names, tradenames, marks, trademarks,
